# ForgeChat — OPTIONAL advanced overrides.
#
# You do NOT need this file for a normal deployment. `docker compose up -d` runs
# with sensible defaults: the backend auto-generates and persists its own secrets
# and connects to the bundled Postgres/Redis. Create a root `.env` (next to
# docker-compose.yml) only if you want to override something below.
#
# Secrets note: JWT_SECRET and FORGECRM_ENCRYPTION_KEY are auto-generated on
# first boot and stored in the `secrets` volume. Set them here ONLY if you want
# to pin specific values — and once data has been encrypted, never change
# FORGECRM_ENCRYPTION_KEY or stored WhatsApp tokens become unreadable.

# ── Infrastructure overrides ────────────────────────────────────────────
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=forgechat        # bundled Postgres password (also in DATABASE_URL via compose)
# HTTP_PORT=8080                     # host port for the web UI
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:forgechat@forgecrm-db:5432/postgres
# REDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379
# JWT_SECRET=                        # auto-generated if unset (openssl rand -hex 32)
# FORGECRM_ENCRYPTION_KEY=           # auto-generated if unset (different from JWT_SECRET)

# ── Optional headless admin seed ────────────────────────────────────────
# If both are set AND no users exist yet, the admin is created on boot and the
# setup wizard is skipped. Otherwise you create the admin in the browser.
# ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.com
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=set-a-strong-password

# ── Meta WhatsApp Cloud API ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# WhatsApp accounts are connected in the UI (Settings → WhatsApp). These are
# optional extras: an app secret to verify inbound webhook signatures, and the
# Graph API version.
# META_APP_SECRET=
# META_API_VERSION=v21.0

# ── Billing / Razorpay (Phase 8) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Organization subscriptions. WITHOUT these, billing order creation returns
# 503 billing-unavailable (fail closed — never a fake order). Verification is
# HMAC-based and always enforced. Get keys from the Razorpay dashboard
# (Test Mode for staging). NEVER expose KEY_SECRET or WEBHOOK_SECRET to the
# frontend — only KEY_ID (public) is returned by the billing API.
# RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
# RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=
# RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# PRICING: no finalized prices exist yet — the server plan catalog uses
# placeholders (see src/billing/plans.js, pricingFinalized=false).

# ── LLM provider fallbacks (AI Agents) ──────────────────────────────────
# Each agent can bring its own key in the UI; these are global fallbacks.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ── Google Primary Authentication (Phase 1) ───────────────────────────
# Google OAuth 2.0 Web Client ID used to verify ID tokens from Google Identity
# Services server-side. Create in Google Cloud Console -> APIs & Services -> Credentials
# with authorized JavaScript origins (e.g. https://app.greenpilot.in, http://localhost:5173).
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-google-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com

# ── Google OAuth (Sheets integration) ──────────────────────────────────
# An admin configures the Google OAuth Client ID, Client Secret, and Redirect URI
# under Settings -> Integrations -> Google; they are stored encrypted in the database.

# ── Other optional tuning (defaults shown) ──────────────────────────────
# MEDIA_TRANSCODE_AUDIO=true         # ffmpeg Ogg→MP3 fallback for Safari
# SEND_RATE_MAX=60                   # outbound messages per SEND_RATE_DURATION_MS
# SEND_RATE_DURATION_MS=1000
# TEMPLATE_SYNC_INTERVAL_MS=600000
